    "result_text": "Build is green.\n\nI implemented the disposable-domain blocklist as a small, self-contained addition following the existing `Reject*` pattern, keeping structural impact minimal \u2014 no existing function was modified:\n\n- **`RejectDisposableEmailDomain`** \u2014 a new single-method function class (WMC_other = 0) that reads the already-normalized email `@Val` and throws when the domain is one of `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`.\n- **`DisposableEmailDomainException`** \u2014 new checked exception.\n- **`DisposableEmailDomainExceptionHandler`** + its escalation YAML \u2014 responds 400, mirroring `InvalidPostcodeException`.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted a `rejectDisposableEmail` step after `normalizeEmail` (which lower-cases/syntax-checks the email first), so the only edit to an existing file is one `next:` retarget plus the new step block.\n\nThe acceptance test `errorRejectsDisposableDomain` and the full suite pass (BUILD SUCCESS).",
